    private_symbol_collision_sshd_four_names_2026-07-28, 1, "2026-11-10 fix-implemented-verification-pending (self-hosted lane, work/p2-private-symbol-collision). Wrong: register_glob_imported_symbols_depth (20.hir/hir_lowering/_Items/module_import_resolution.spl) registered every globbed callable/constant as Public with last-write-wins binding, so a private fn/val reached via `use m.*` silently displaced the importer's earlier binding of the same name from another module (public or private) and the bare-name call mis-dispatched to whichever module was globbed last. Fix: glob_private_would_displace -- a private glob item may fill an unbound name (tolerated leak, interp_private_names_selfhost_check_2026-11-09, 20124 src baseline pairs untouched) but never overwrites a binding owned by a different module; own declarations still win (declared after imports); public globs unchanged; types were already first-write-wins. Spec test/01_unit/compiler/35.semantics/private_glob_import_module_local_resolution_spec.spl: red 3/6 failed (expected pb to equal pa) -> green 6/6. Neighbours explicit_import_beats_glob_reexport_spec 2/2, hir_glob_reachable_miss_memo_spec 5/5; imported_tuple_signature_dependency_spec 6/7 and resolve_methods_quiet_typed_spec 1/4 fail identically with the change stashed (pre-existing). Seed C1/C2 (Rust lowering_core.rs dedup key, candidates.last() fallback) still open; native verification pending."

